    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0651" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/>

                <head>No. 248.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_CEDL1"
                            type="from">De Long</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-12-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 21, 1872</date>. (Received
                        Jan. 23, 1873.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 324.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that on
                    yesterday I received from the minister for foreign affairs of this empire a
                    note, (inclosure No. 1) advising me that this government has changed its
                    calendar and adopted the system in use in America and Europe; to which I this
                    day replied by a note (inclosure No. 2) congratulating him upon this reform.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <persName corresp="#p_CEDL1">C. E. DE LONG.</persName>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d251-a1.xml" xpointer="d251-a1"/>
